{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1381295-questions-about-cru\u00e1c","id":1381295,"title":"Questions about Cru\u00e1c","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-14T05:45:20-07:00","id":1381295,"title":"Questions about Cru\u00e1c","content":"I have many questions about Cru\u00e1c. I already searched on topics, but most of them are about VtR 1ed, so I thought about and decided to create this topic.<br /> <br /> 1 - How does one affect someone else via Blood Sympathy? Like, with a Ghoul or Child from the target.<br /> 2 - Is it possible to affect other people with rituals that target the caster using Blood Sympathy?<br /> 3 - Is there a way, without using Blasphemys and Sacraments, to use a improvised Cru\u00e1c rite in a single turn, instead of a extended action?<br /> 4 - Can I plant a seed from my Mandragora Garden elsewhere, to use it as a proxy for my rituals, or my Garden needs to be in a single Safe Place?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T09:02:32-07:00","id":1381336,"title":"","content":"1. You don't unless a specific ritual specifies it. (And I don't know of any that do.) The only thing Blood Sympathy does is adding bonus dice to Discipline usages. How much for each step is stated in the Blood Sympathy rules in the core book.<br /> 2. No.<br /> 3. Generally no. There's a Bloodline in the CotC book that has an inherent ritual they can activate with a single action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T09:24:28-07:00","id":1381344,"title":"","content":"<br /> 1. Blood sympathy rules are on p. 98 and 99. It mostly entails detecting general location, mood, emotion, and status of a kindred based on the outlined connections and a limited form of telepathy. Specific Cruac rituals targetting someone who shares blood sympathy can double the blood sympathy dice bonuses based on how far removed they count for purposes of casting range etc. Unless the ghoul has the merit establishing blood sympathy to their regnant, it doesn\u2019t mechanically exist. If the caster has a direct line of descent to their target, the dice bonuses based on the line of descent is doubled. (Sire/childe is +6 instead of +3)<br /> <br /> 2. Unless some special magical toy or merit or the ritual expressly says otherwise, you can\u2019t use someone who shares a blood sympathy to the intended target as a conduit to hit them with the spell. (All members of the same clan share blood sympathy to another of their clan. They just don\u2019t get bonus dice to access it.)<br /> Loosely translated: Some Daeva Acolyte hag in San Francisco, California is not casting Pangs of Prosperina on a Mekhet she grabbed off the street and imprisoned in order to target a Mekhet Acolyte hag in Salem Massachusetts. Said Daeva, however, could potentially target her own grandchilde for joining the Lancea et Sanctum from a further distance than say, the neonate Gangrel childe of the hierophant for the same offense.<br /> <br /> 3. That\u2019s ST\u2019s fiat. I allow for a few rituals to be made a \u201csignature ritual\u201d via homebrew merit that allows it to be cast in a single turn. Those can potentially be interrupted or disrupted in the turn. Or precast as an extended action at the start of the night and the effects held to be released as an instant action and cannot be usually be Celerity interrupted but still resisted.<br /> <br /> 4. That\u2019s ST\u2019s fiat. I\u2019d say no in most cases because Mandragora are high maintenance plants that die quickly without regular vitae infusions so you aren\u2019t going to plant a mandragora bomb in someone\u2019s azaleas that\u2019s going to go unnoticed. I \u201cdid\u201d have an NPC routinely gift mandragora plants to her PC childe in order to protect her using Theban Sorcery rituals. The childe knew to feed it vitae regularly but the mandragora still died and had to be replaced occasionally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}